A||||1||Alex2004||drive axle noise under semi-hard acceleration???||||5||
Z||000000||Alex2004||11-09-2001||05:28 PM||||I have an 84 SE w/ 96*** miles on it and now whenver i'm accelerating i hear kind of a clicking/rattling noise i'm guessing it's coming from the drive axle's.  I only hear it during higher rpm's during hard accleration, also whenever i'm acclerating from a stop and turning at the same time the car will sorta shake.  Do you know what causing this?  And can i grease the drive axle's like in the boots?  Are there grease fittings on them?  LMK, thanks...<P>Alex...||||reg||5
Z||000001||johnt671||11-09-2001||06:16 PM||||On acceleration the inner CV joint rumble when bad, and the outer CV joints clicking on turns means they are bad.  No grease fittings and no way to repack them without at least partly getting the boot off.  I've seen small grease needles that may let you inject some grease in the boot but never tried it.  Bad news is you need to replace the bad axle or axles,  Good news is they usually go for awhile when they start making noise.  If your car is shaking from the bad axle it is probably replacement time.||||reg||1
